Subject: [PATCH 4/6] binder: the hwbinder backport, replayed from LineageOS kenzo

Android 8 split binder into three domains -- /dev/binder, /dev/hwbinder and
/dev/vndbinder -- and HIDL, which is how Android 9 reaches every HAL, talks over
the second one with protocol features this kernel does not have: scatter-gather
buffers (BC_TRANSACTION_SG, BINDER_TYPE_PTR) and file-descriptor arrays
(BINDER_TYPE_FDA). The ASUS kernel has neither, and a single misc device.

The first version of this patch gave the kernel the three devices only (Google's
multiple-context-manager commits) and stopped there. The devices appeared, so it
looked done; the first LineageOS 16 boot showed it was not. Every HIDL service
died on registerAsService() with UNKNOWN_ERROR (-2147483648), keystore aborted
with "Failed to get ServiceManager", healthd -- a critical service -- crashed
four times in four minutes and init sent the tablet to the bootloader. The
transactions libhwbinder sends are scatter-gather ones, and this driver did not
understand them.

Two ways of getting the rest were tried. Applying the remaining commits from
Google's deprecated/android-3.10 branch on top failed on 11 hunks and put others
hundreds of lines away with fuzz 2: that branch is Google's, and this binder.c
is Qualcomm CAF's, and the differences compound commit after commit. Writing the
difference by hand on an IPC driver was ruled out from the start.

What works is LineageOS' kernel for the Xiaomi Redmi Note 3 Pro (kenzo,
android_kernel_xiaomi_msm8956, branch lineage-15.0): the same SoC, the same CAF
3.10 base, and Android 8 on it, which already needs hwbinder. Its binder.c just
before the series (f21ae653664) differs from the ASUS one by three lines of
whitespace in one printk. Its 14 commits, replayed in order on the ASUS files,
apply with no conflicts at all:

  ebda70d8de7  android: binder: split flat_binder_object.
  b3ecf66ab62  Add security hooks to binder and implement the hooks for SELinux.
  4173ab8d231  android: binder: support multiple context managers.
  b7436eb0f5e  android: binder: deal with contexts in debugfs.
  750e5a75ffb  android: binder: support multiple /dev instances.
  92d725523b2  android: binder: refactor binder_transact()
  3ef58fa8896  android: binder: add extra size to allocator.
  39afd75d055  android: binder: support for scatter-gather.
  c20fae82a06  android: binder: support for file-descriptor arrays.
  47d8ab2cee8  android: binder: use copy_from_user_preempt_disabled
  5cc63ca36dc  UPSTREAM: drivers: android: correct the size of struct
               binder_uintptr_t for BC_DEAD_BINDER_DONE
  a2d1aa626cb  binder: use group leader instead of open thread
  8eb72fd11d1  android: binder: Use wake up hint for synchronous transactions.
  68069e40e86  android: binder: Disable preemption while holding the global
               binder lock.

and the result is kenzo's files exactly: binder.h byte for byte, binder.c but
for those three lines of whitespace. b3ecf66 is Stephen Smalley's upstream
binder LSM hooks (Linux 3.14); it is why the old patch's one failed hunk failed
(upstream calls security_binder_set_context_mgr(), this tree did not), and the
SELinux binder class it implements is what Android's policy is written against.

The defconfig sets CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_DEVICES="binder,hwbinder,vndbinder".
The Kconfig default stays "binder", so this changes nothing for anyone who does
not ask for it.
